/*
 * Declares the OptionFieldAccessValue class.
 *
 * OptionFieldAccessValue represents a pseudo-field access on an option value.
 * Options expose two semantic fields:
 *
 *   - `value`     — returns the wrapped value and throws if the option is empty;
 *   - `hasValue`  — returns a boolean indicating whether the option contains a value.
 *
 * These accesses are not structural field accesses: they correspond to semantic
 * operations defined by the Option type. None of them produce an lvalue.

 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::fields::option
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/fields/option.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-03-02
